  "findings": [
    "Private fixed-path canonical parses, private guard identity/mode/digest keys, stable evaluator identity, independent mutable result copies, and per-edge predecessor/successor assertions were verified. Supplied values never gain canonical memo eligibility.",
    "Inherited-prototype hook classification and custom-reader this-binding findings were corrected before the reviewed v2 freeze. Independent probes confirm opaque fallback parity and no owner-state disclosure.",
    "All supported wrappers finalize; internal helpers are trusted implementation, not a hostile same-process-importer sandbox. No application/package re-export or supported callback/context API was added.",
    "Every consumed input is finally reread. The terminal uses 597 paths; source/NTMI also consume an older browser README, making 598 paths. Independent post-capture mutation and deletion probes cover that extra input.",
    "Sequential observations are non-atomic. Mutate/restore between first and final reads, or mutation after a path final read, can evade detection. Tests demonstrate both limits; no release lock is claimed.",
    "All prior assertions and exact historical branches remain, apart from accepted exact PR43 terminal forwarding and the NTMI owner-bound initial read. Published approvals, immutable source/UI evidence, dependencies, workflows, budgets, and audit policy remain unchanged.",
    "The supplied-invalid-reader contract is now preserved: only omitted built-in reader configuration receives an eager callability check. Explicit invalid readers retain no-read success and original predicate/accessor error order; an actual legacy read raises the original native TypeError. All105 independently compared outcomes/traces matched frozen41c37d. Optimized default-reader semantics and all admission predicates are unchanged."
